{
  "case_id": "2009-08-911",
  "document_hash": "8444d33056dc66d0498cd44e3f1122a57e51cea1876645cfc6eb8c73a8eadfee",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2009-08-911",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8444d33056dc66d0498cd44e3f1122a57e51cea1876645cfc6eb8c73a8eadfee",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8444d33056dc-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:04 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2009-08-911",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8444d33056dc66d0498cd44e3f1122a57e51cea1876645cfc6eb8c73a8eadfee",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8444d33056dc-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. SCHOENFIELD: Mr. Chief Justice, and may\nit please the Court:\nIn enacting section 1252(a)(2)(B), Congress\nlimited its reduction of judicial review to where the\nauthority for the Attorney General's discretion is\nspecified under subchapter 2 of chapter 12 of Title 8.\nCongress did not express any intent to\nremove the courts\u2019 jurisdiction to review discretionary\ndecisions, the authority for which is specified under\nany other subchapter or in regulations, nor did Congress\nexpress any intent to delegate its constitutional\nresponsibility to determine Federal jurisdiction to the\nAttorney General --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2009-08-911",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8444d33056dc66d0498cd44e3f1122a57e51cea1876645cfc6eb8c73a8eadfee",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8444d33056dc-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: How does that -- how does\nthat read? I -- I recall the briefs say that, but I don't recall reading it. Is it -- does it appear somewhere?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2009-08-911",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8444d33056dc66d0498cd44e3f1122a57e51cea1876645cfc6eb8c73a8eadfee",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8444d33056dc-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Oh, I'm asking you, what possible sense could it make?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2009-08-911",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8444d33056dc66d0498cd44e3f1122a57e51cea1876645cfc6eb8c73a8eadfee",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8444d33056dc-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Oh, by the way, this reopening is done by regulation, not done by statute."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Department of Justice",
      "case_id": "2009-08-911",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8444d33056dc66d0498cd44e3f1122a57e51cea1876645cfc6eb8c73a8eadfee",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8444d33056dc-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. SAHARSKY: There are only a handful of\ncases, and in those cases, several individual attorneys\nargued that there was no jurisdiction. And as soon as\nthe leadership of the Office of Immigration Litigation\nheard of those cases, it sat down with the text of the\nstatute and said: We think that the text here is clear,\nand we don't think the jurisdiction is taken away."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2009-08-911",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8444d33056dc66d0498cd44e3f1122a57e51cea1876645cfc6eb8c73a8eadfee",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8444d33056dc-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 29,
        "start": 29
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: I didn't do the math fast enough in my head when you were answering Justice Kennedy's question, but is he correct that the effect of accepting your argument is about 2,000 additional appeals that -- that the Department of Justice will have to brief and the courts of appeals will have to decide?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2009-08-911",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8444d33056dc66d0498cd44e3f1122a57e51cea1876645cfc6eb8c73a8eadfee",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8444d33056dc-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Do you want to say anything about, apparently, this idiosyncratic thought that I have had?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2009-08-911",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8444d33056dc66d0498cd44e3f1122a57e51cea1876645cfc6eb8c73a8eadfee",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8444d33056dc-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Is there any rhyme or reason why some universe of things that could be reviewed in court, Congress put some of the them in the statute and left others out?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2009-08-911",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8444d33056dc66d0498cd44e3f1122a57e51cea1876645cfc6eb8c73a8eadfee",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8444d33056dc-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: May I ask this question before you finish -- if it is an appropriate time?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2009-08-911",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8444d33056dc66d0498cd44e3f1122a57e51cea1876645cfc6eb8c73a8eadfee",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8444d33056dc-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 50,
        "start": 50
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Do you have any reason why Congress would have taken great trouble to make certain that courts can review asylum decisions, but Congress would not have wanted a court to review a reopening of an asylum matter, which can be done, after all, only if something new comes up that justifies asylum?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2009-08-911",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8444d33056dc66d0498cd44e3f1122a57e51cea1876645cfc6eb8c73a8eadfee",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8444d33056dc-0002-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. SCHOENFIELD: Section 1252(b)(6) mandates that review of the underlying decision should be consolidated with review of a motion to reopen. I think that tells us several things. The first and foremost of which is Congress intended there to be review of motions to reopen -- at least some motions to reopen."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2009-08-911",
      "confidence": 0.0,
